00:00:00.122 --> 00:00:01.394
- Good morning, Believe Nation,

00:00:01.394 --> 00:00:04.305
my name is Evan Carmichael,
my one one is believe,

00:00:04.305 --> 00:00:06.677
and I believe entrepreneurs
are going to solve

00:00:06.677 --> 00:00:09.353
all of the world's major problems.

00:00:09.353 --> 00:00:10.562
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:10.562 --> 00:00:13.869
today, we're going to learn
how to be your real self

00:00:13.869 --> 00:00:15.369
over the UKRS-One.

00:00:18.988 --> 00:00:21.650
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.342
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:24.342 --> 00:00:27.842
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:28.697 --> 00:00:31.114
- If you can be a better you,

00:00:32.737 --> 00:00:35.320
success is in the back of that.

00:00:37.266 --> 00:00:38.514
I'll say it again.

00:00:38.514 --> 00:00:39.768
Make sure you get this, brother,

00:00:39.768 --> 00:00:43.601
'cause you all need to
listen to me right now.

00:00:44.841 --> 00:00:46.424
Success is based on

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.407
you being you.

00:00:52.117 --> 00:00:54.700
If you can't be your real self,

00:00:56.238 --> 00:00:58.071
success is impossible.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:03.410
A fake you can never be successful.

00:01:04.938 --> 00:01:08.188
Only a real you is going to be successful.

00:01:09.116 --> 00:01:12.152
- I 100% agree that you will only have

00:01:12.152 --> 00:01:14.776
your real success when
you find your real self

00:01:14.776 --> 00:01:16.658
and you apply it and you take action on it

00:01:16.658 --> 00:01:17.708
every single day.

00:01:17.708 --> 00:01:20.395
You can model, you could copy,
you could learn from others,

00:01:20.395 --> 00:01:23.669
to get somewhere faster,
but you will never reach

00:01:23.669 --> 00:01:25.925
your true potential by
being a junior version

00:01:25.925 --> 00:01:28.017
of somebody else.

00:01:28.017 --> 00:01:29.880
I had an entrepreneur
friend of mine reach out,

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.476
she started a new business, she was one

00:01:31.476 --> 00:01:35.599
of the top trainers at
a gym here hin Canada.

00:01:35.599 --> 00:01:38.197
And she wanted to go
teach that training system

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:40.438
to other people, basically
take the training

00:01:40.438 --> 00:01:42.376
that she learned from the big corporate

00:01:42.376 --> 00:01:45.864
and apply it and help smaller
gyms do their training.

00:01:45.864 --> 00:01:49.447
Using that model, all
she would be at best,

00:01:50.697 --> 00:01:54.047
is a junior version of the big corporate.

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.238
So if somebody, as an example,

00:01:55.238 --> 00:01:58.064
studying under Tony Robbins, and goes out

00:01:58.064 --> 00:02:02.119
and applies his strategies
to help other people,

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:05.084
if you don't build on it,
if you don't improve on it

00:02:05.084 --> 00:02:06.455
then all you're going to be at best

00:02:06.455 --> 00:02:07.926
is a junior Tony Robbins.

00:02:07.926 --> 00:02:09.488
You're going to be a
poor man's Tony Robbin.

00:02:09.488 --> 00:02:11.701
So if somebody can't afford
Tony, they would come to you.

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:14.060
You can be so much more
than a junior version

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:15.387
of somebody else.

00:02:15.387 --> 00:02:19.639
And so yes, you model, and
you copy, and you learn

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:22.702
to get ideas, to test,
to try to implement,

00:02:22.702 --> 00:02:26.702
and then to tweak and
improve and make your own.

00:02:28.283 --> 00:02:29.475
So as an example, when I was working

00:02:29.475 --> 00:02:32.308
with my agent and my media trainer,

00:02:32.308 --> 00:02:34.851
they would always give
me assignments every week

00:02:34.851 --> 00:02:37.381
and say, "Evan, your next
video you have to do this."

00:02:37.381 --> 00:02:39.540
Try this, try this, give
me different assignments

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:43.229
and Steve came at it
from a very aggressive,

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:45.482
you've got to raise the stakes, you've got

00:02:45.482 --> 00:02:46.750
to make it more important point of view

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.171
and Janie came at it
from a more connection,

00:02:49.171 --> 00:02:51.722
love and soft point of
view, and they would always

00:02:51.722 --> 00:02:52.607
give me assignments.

00:02:52.607 --> 00:02:54.510
And every assignment they gave me,

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:57.830
never quite hit, always
felt uncomfortable.

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:01.080
I would do it, I would do it
like they wanted me to do it,

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.387
and I never quite fully connected.

00:03:04.387 --> 00:03:05.968
It was a stretch, it was better

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:07.123
than what I was currently doing,

00:03:07.123 --> 00:03:09.041
but it wasn't quite what I needed.

00:03:09.041 --> 00:03:11.587
And I always had to take their advice

00:03:11.587 --> 00:03:13.765
and tweak it a little bit,

00:03:13.765 --> 00:03:18.545
and build on it, and grow it,
to make it feel right for me.

00:03:18.545 --> 00:03:20.151
And so every time you're
learning these strategies

00:03:20.151 --> 00:03:21.286
that I'm sharing on this channel,

00:03:21.286 --> 00:03:23.599
you're learning from Steve
Jobs, or Oprah Winfrey,

00:03:23.599 --> 00:03:25.329
or whoever it is that you look up to

00:03:25.329 --> 00:03:28.971
and want to be a huge success,
your goal should never be

00:03:28.971 --> 00:03:31.843
to be the next Steve
Jobs or Oprah Winfrey,

00:03:31.843 --> 00:03:34.987
your goal is to be the
best version of yourself.

00:03:34.987 --> 00:03:37.146
And you do that by modeling others

00:03:37.146 --> 00:03:40.037
and learning from them, and
then tweaking the strategies

00:03:40.037 --> 00:03:42.531
so that it fits for you.

00:03:42.531 --> 00:03:43.868
So the question of the day today is,

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:46.230
I'm curious, what is one
thing that you've learned

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:48.892
from somebody successful,
or somebody on this channel,

00:03:48.892 --> 00:03:51.519
and then tweaked their
strategy to make it work

00:03:51.519 --> 00:03:53.409
in your business.

00:03:53.409 --> 00:03:54.982
Leave it down on the comments below,

00:03:54.982 --> 00:03:56.353
I'm super curious to find out.

00:03:56.353 --> 00:03:58.240
I also want to give a
quick shout out to Ariel.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.626
Ariel, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:04:00.626 --> 00:04:03.360
Your One Word, I really,
really appreciate it

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:05.537
and I really hope you're
enjoying the read.

00:04:05.537 --> 00:04:06.511
So thank you guys again for watching,

00:04:06.511 --> 00:04:07.842
I believe in you.

00:04:07.842 --> 00:04:09.883
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:04:09.883 --> 00:04:13.078
and whatever your one word is, much love,

00:04:13.078 --> 00:04:14.575
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:04:14.575 --> 00:04:17.350
for another shot of Entspresso.

