♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:08:16.184 --> 00:08:17.301
- What do you want to say to your fans

00:08:17.301 --> 00:08:19.377
that ask you like, yo, are
you still going to make

00:08:19.377 --> 00:08:22.311
that high BPM, you know, festival music,

00:08:22.311 --> 00:08:25.309
to Lee, are you leaving that for more --

00:08:25.309 --> 00:08:26.299
- I'm not leaving anything.

00:08:26.299 --> 00:08:28.299
- Midstreamer, can you
explain that transition

00:08:28.299 --> 00:08:29.440
and what you're doing there?

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:33.271
- For me it's all about
trying to find new sounds,

00:08:33.271 --> 00:08:35.052
reinventing your own sound.

00:08:35.052 --> 00:08:36.802
I can release 128 BPM

00:08:38.474 --> 00:08:40.094
club song every week,

00:08:40.094 --> 00:08:42.497
but I don't know, I want
to challenge myself too,

00:08:42.497 --> 00:08:44.550
I want to try out new
things, I want to experiment,

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:47.143
and me trying something
new and doing something

00:08:47.143 --> 00:08:48.939
like Scared to be Lonely
and In the Name of Love

00:08:48.939 --> 00:08:50.513
doesn't mean I'm completely
switching my sound.

00:08:50.513 --> 00:08:53.763
In October, I just released seven

00:08:53.763 --> 00:08:57.367
very aggressive 128 BPM house songs

00:08:57.367 --> 00:08:59.542
and I've got Ultra coming up,

00:08:59.542 --> 00:09:00.500
I've got Coachella coming up,

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:02.095
and I'm also going to play a lot of

00:09:02.095 --> 00:09:03.529
old sounding Martin Garrix.

00:09:03.529 --> 00:09:06.280
It's a weird situation,
because then I released

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:09.178
a house song one year
ago and they're like,

00:09:09.178 --> 00:09:12.011
"Oh, same repetitive boring stuff.

00:09:13.533 --> 00:09:15.493
"Do something new, be refreshing."

00:09:15.493 --> 00:09:17.076
And I do something new and they're like,

00:09:17.076 --> 00:09:18.227
"We miss the old Martin Garrix."

00:09:18.227 --> 00:09:20.611
And I'm like, wait, what
do you guys want me to do?

00:09:20.611 --> 00:09:22.991
But for me, what I
think is most important,

00:09:22.991 --> 00:09:25.232
is just me being myself in the studio.

00:09:25.232 --> 00:09:28.102
Doing what I want and don't let

00:09:28.102 --> 00:09:30.488
other people's opinions affect my music.

00:09:30.488 --> 00:09:33.783
I want to represent what I want to make

00:09:33.783 --> 00:09:35.939
and I'm not switching my sound,

00:09:35.939 --> 00:09:37.306
I'm just having fun.

00:09:37.306 --> 00:09:39.344
- I live for the quiet moments

00:09:39.344 --> 00:09:41.537
where I can be my most authentic self

00:09:41.537 --> 00:09:42.972
and hear myself think.

00:09:42.972 --> 00:09:44.863
Somebody asked me, "What makes you happy?"

00:09:44.863 --> 00:09:46.760
My husband said, "Bacon."

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:48.870
(audience laughing)

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:49.720
Which is true.

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:52.349
(audience laughing)

00:09:52.349 --> 00:09:55.831
I'm the happiest when I'm
my most authentic self.

00:09:55.831 --> 00:09:59.374
When nobody's looking,
when nobody's judging me,

00:09:59.374 --> 00:10:03.570
when nobody's leaving nasty
comments on my (mumbles),

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:05.320
and I can just exist.

00:10:07.218 --> 00:10:10.218
And in that quiet space, I realized,

00:10:11.174 --> 00:10:13.424
I am worthy by birth right.

00:10:15.646 --> 00:10:19.229
I am fierce and fabulous
because I breathe.

00:10:20.185 --> 00:10:22.518
All of us here in this room,

00:10:23.967 --> 00:10:26.300
we are worthy, we are valid.

00:10:27.393 --> 00:10:30.560
Our journeys are real and worth while.

00:10:33.581 --> 00:10:35.468
And there is nothing that anyone can do

00:10:35.468 --> 00:10:37.055
to take that away from us.

00:10:37.055 --> 00:10:39.457
Everything terrible
that has happened to us,

00:10:39.457 --> 00:10:41.984
we have a choice at how we ought to react.

00:10:41.984 --> 00:10:43.733
A lot of times, what
we're actually reacting to

00:10:43.733 --> 00:10:45.983
is the fear of humiliation,

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:51.408
the fear of what are they
going to think about me?

00:10:51.408 --> 00:10:54.290
The fear of possible judgment.

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:55.356
Newsflash, people will judge you

00:10:55.356 --> 00:10:57.594
whether you discover the cure for cancer

00:10:57.594 --> 00:10:59.261
or sit on the couch.

00:11:00.786 --> 00:11:02.703
You might as well live.

00:11:04.782 --> 00:11:05.782
I am a wife,

00:11:07.987 --> 00:11:10.320
but that does not define me.

00:11:11.762 --> 00:11:14.357
I am an actress, and that as sure as hell

00:11:14.357 --> 00:11:16.290
does not define me.

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:18.623
I'm a parent, while awesome,

00:11:20.461 --> 00:11:22.628
that is not my whole life.

00:11:23.568 --> 00:11:25.423
None of those things,
even though I get a lot

00:11:25.423 --> 00:11:28.423
of praise for that, makes me worthy.

00:11:30.363 --> 00:11:33.444
I am worthy by birth right,

00:11:33.444 --> 00:11:35.611
I am Gabrielle Union Wade.

